<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45271" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Statielli</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Statelli</span></b> ), ōrum, m.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of
				Liguria</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 7, § 47</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 42,
				21</span></i>.—<i>Their chief town</i> was
			called Aquae Statiellorum, Plin. l. l.; or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Statĭellae</span></b> ,
			ārum, f., <i><span class="en">id. 31, 2, 2, §
			4</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sta-tiellas</span></b> ,
				ātis, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Statielli</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					42, 7</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sta-tiellātes</span></b> ,
			ĭum, m., <i><span class="en">Liv. 42,
			8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">42,
			21</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Statiellenses</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of</i> Aquae Statiellorum, Brut. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				11, 11, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
